{"id":21,"date":"2012-11-26T00:37:01","date_gmt":"2012-11-26T08:37:01","guid":{"rendered":"http:\/\/ccra.us\/wordpress\/?page_id=21"},"modified":"2023-02-21T13:33:27","modified_gmt":"2023-02-21T21:33:27","slug":"bald-peak","status":"publish","type":"page","link":"http:\/\/ccra.us\/coverage\/bald-peak\/","title":{"rendered":"Bald Peak"},"content":{"rendered":"<p>The WA6HAM Repeater system operates three VHF repeaters from three different radio sites located in Contra Costa County. Kregor Peak, Bald Peak and Highland Peak radio sites provide portable radio coverage for 3 distinct areas of the County that are separated by geographic regions. The repeaters normally are linked together but can be separated for special operational requirements.<\/p>\n<p>Below are the coverage maps for Bald Peak. A coverage map displays signal strength using colors. The hotter the color the stronger the radio signal.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Bald Peak<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><strong>145.49 MHz (-600 KHz); PL 107.2 Hz &#8211; <\/strong>Bald Peak is located in wester Contra Costa County between the cities of Orinda and Berkeley.\u00a0 The altitude of the radio site is @1900 ft and has a commanding view of the central county cities of Lafayette, Moraga and Orinda.\u00a0 Towards the west it sees west County cities of Richmond, El Cerrito, Hercules, San Pablo, Pinole, El Sobrante, Crockett and Rodeo.\u00a0 Beyond the Contra Costa cities lies the entire Oakland-San Francisco Bay Area.<\/p>\n\n\t\t<style type=\"text\/css\">\n\t\t\t#gallery-1 {\n\t\t\t\tmargin: auto;\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t#gallery-1 .gallery-item {\n\t\t\t\tfloat: left;\n\t\t\t\tmargin-top: 10px;\n\t\t\t\ttext-align: center;\n\t\t\t\twidth: 25%;\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t#gallery-1 img {\n\t\t\t\tborder: 2px solid #cfcfcf;\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t#gallery-1 .gallery-caption {\n\t\t\t\tmargin-left: 0;\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\/* see gallery_shortcode() in wp-includes\/media.php *\/\n\t\t<\/style>\n\t\t<div data-carousel-extra='{\"blog_id\":1,\"permalink\":\"http:\\\/\\\/ccra.